{
  "question": "the gate carries a residual budget of 60 proteins the annotation calls a beta subunit but which are not classified as beta. Why?",
  "what_the_roadmap_said": "that one of the two was wrong -- the annotation or the model set -- and that which one had not been measured",
  "what_the_measurement_says": "neither. None of the 60 has a row in neighbor_protein, so no model was ever given a sequence to match. A statement about an unscanned sequence is not a statement about the annotation",
  "method": {
    "source": "the CDS feature in the GenBank record itself",
    "coordinates": "the database stores BioPython's 0-based half-open range while GenBank writes 1-based inclusive, so the feature is looked up at start+1..end; without that conversion the record is not found at all, which is what happened on the first attempt",
    "changes_nothing": "classification, gate budget and tables are untouched; this measures and reports"
  },
